# IMAGE ASSETS GO THROUGH GIT LFS.
#
# The repo carries ~13 MB of art that was uploaded to Roblox (badges, icon,
# passes, store banners) plus reference and documentation shots. Those are the
# exact bytes the platform received and are worth keeping — but they are
# binary, they never diff usefully, and every revision of one is a full copy in
# the pack. LFS keeps the working tree identical and the history light.
# What is NOT here is just as deliberate: developer render output is gitignored
# rather than stored (see .gitignore), so this rule only ever applies to art
# somebody chose to keep.
# NOTE: this converts files from the commit that adds it onward. History is not
# rewritten — the old blobs stay where they are, which costs nothing further
# and avoids forcing every clone to re-fetch.
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpeg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.gif filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.webp filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Roblox binary model/place files are the same story.
*.rbxm filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.rbxl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# Audio sources rendered by roblox/render-audio.mjs and uploaded to Roblox.
*.wav filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ogg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
